  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Metro Line",
    "overview": "A trip is a metro line. Cities are stations; the route is one thick magenta line that grows a station each time a city is added. The ground is plain white (deep night-blue in dark), the ink near-black, and every heading reads like a station sign: condensed, bold, upper case. It replaces the card-list-over-a-map habit of travel apps with the diagram itself.\n\nThe signature is the line drawing down to a new station: when a city is committed, the segment above it grows from the top and the station's ring pops (overshoots, then settles). It plays only under `motion-safe`; reduced motion shows the placed station at once.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One route colour, one line, ringed stations, a dashed open station for \"next\".",
      "Colours have jobs: line, people, time. Nothing else is coloured.",
      "Flat signboards with a 2px ink rule; no shadows on the page.",
      "Condensed upper-case display over a plain, legible body face."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Colours Have Jobs Rule",
        "body": "Magenta is the route and the brand, teal is people, amber is time. Do not use one for another's job, and never colour a heading.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Button Rule",
        "body": "The primary button is ink, not magenta, so the line colour stays with the route. It turns line-coloured on hover.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Station Sign Rule",
        "body": "Anything that names a place or a trip is set in the display face; anything that explains is set in Onest.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Stations Are the Controls Rule",
        "body": "On a form, the city fields are the stations: each is an Input with the station appearance inside a route-stop, and the date sits in that station's meta as a time chip. Do not build a form beside the line and a picture of the line next to it.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do show a trip as its line, cities as stations, in order.",
